433 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 34 0 R
/T (FY25 PAT rose 54.7% to KES 75.5bn, but the mix of the rise matters more than the headline. Of the KES 31.4bn increase in profit before tax, KES 18.2bn came from net interest income, KES 5.7bn from non-interest income, KES 5.7bn from lower provisions and KES 1.7bn from lower operating costs. Income therefore explains about 76% of the rise and the recovery is not just a provisions release.)
/E (FY25 PAT rose 54.7% to KES 75.5bn, but the mix of the rise matters more than the headline. Of the KES 31.4bn increase in profit before tax, KES 18.2bn came from net interest income, KES 5.7bn from non-interest income, KES 5.7bn from lower provisions and KES 1.7bn from lower operating costs. Income therefore explains about 76% of the rise and the recovery is not just a provisions release.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [51]
>>
endobj
434 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 34 0 R
/T (Interest income grew 2.0% while interest expense fell 24.2%, so most of the KES 18.2bn NII gain came from cheaper funding, not bigger earning assets. Part of that should last, but it is why the base case uses a 22% ROE and not 26.4%.)
