/Title (The cross-checks bracket the target. Peer P/E gives KES 102 but FY25 EPS is flattered by low provisions, so it is treated as an upper bound. Peer P/B gives KES 79 and the dividend-yield method KES 62, but both ignore that Equity earns more on its book and pays out only 30% of profit. The valuation methods are not averaged to determine the target price.)
