/Title (FY25 PAT rose 54.7% to KES 75.5bn, but the mix of the rise matters more than the headline. Of the KES 31.4bn increase in profit before tax, KES 18.2bn came from net interest income, KES 5.7bn from non-interest income, KES 5.7bn from lower provisions and KES 1.7bn from lower operating costs. Income therefore explains about 76% of the rise and the recovery is not just a provisions release.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2080 0 R
/First 2181 0 R
/Last 2182 0 R
/Count -10
/Next 2130 0 R
>>
endobj
2130 0 obj
<<
/Title (Interest income grew 2.0% while interest expense fell 24.2%, so most of the KES 18.2bn NII gain came from cheaper funding, not bigger earning assets. Part of that should last, but it is why the base case uses a 22% ROE and not 26.4%.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2080 0 R
/Prev 2129 0 R
>>
