/Title (Earnings quality. FY25 profit before tax rose by KES 31.4bn compared to FY24. Higher income accounts for about 76% of that, lower provisions 18% and lower operating costs 6%. We do not treat FY25 as a run-rate. Net interest income grew 16.8% while interest income grew only 2.0%; the difference was a 24.2% fall in interest expense as deposit costs eased. That is why the base case uses a 22% ROE and not 26.4%.)
/Dest [10 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2071 0 R
/Prev 2169 0 R
/Next 2119 0 R
>>
